      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The pressure you feel is immense, and it’s completely understandable that you feel trapped by the expectations of others. But you are not a machine, and you deserve to feel something other than dread. Sometimes, the only way to stop the loop is to break it, and a small, deliberate act of self-care is the first step toward reclaiming your own space. Even five minutes of genuine quiet, without the pressure to \"fix\" anything, can be a radical act of rebellion against that relentless cycle.",
      "source": "target",
